at has the Bulldogs at No. 1 in the CFP rankings, agreed to a five-year deal to become the next coach at Florida State, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T02:51:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4916996/ahmad-moten-sr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Moten_Sr."},"pick":{"pick":48,"round":2,"team":"NE","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ahmad Moten Sr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Moten_Sr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:13Z","intro":"Ahmad Moten Sr. (born April 22, 2004) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Moten Sr. attended Cardinal Gibbons High School in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. As a senior he had 39 tackles and three sacks. He committed to the University of Miami to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Moten Sr. played in two games and reshirted his first year at Miami in 2022. He played in 11 games and had two tackles with one interception as a redshirt freshman in 2023 and started two of 11 games, recording 18 tackles with one sack as a redshirt sophomore in 2024. Moten Sr. returned to Miami as a starter his redshirt junior year in 2025."}]}}